{%- doc -%}
  Black Friday switch (Theme settings > Black Friday, docs/launch/black-friday-switch.md).

  Rendered in the <head>. When the switch is on (or the theme editor preview is ticked) this sets
  <html data-bf="live"> before anything paints, once the start time has passed by the visitor's
  clock, or by the server's when the page was rendered after the start. Shopify caches storefront
  pages, so a Liquid date check alone would keep serving the "before" page for a while after the
  start; the browser check flips every page on time, cached or not.

  Every Black Friday extra is only output when the switch is on, and carries one of:
  - data-bf-on: shown only while live
  - data-bf-off: hidden while live (the old Sale menu link, the normal sale page title)
  The hero's Black Friday slide is taken out by assets/coszus-home.js when it isn't live.

  Switch off: none of this is output and the site is exactly as before.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign bf_preview = false
  if request.design_mode and settings.bf_editor_preview
    assign bf_preview = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if settings.bf_enabled or bf_preview -%}
  {%- liquid
    capture bf_start
      render 'coszus-bf-start'
    endcapture
    assign bf_start = bf_start | plus: 0
    assign now_ts = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign bf_server_live = false
    if bf_preview
      assign bf_server_live = true
    elsif bf_start > 0 and now_ts >= bf_start
      assign bf_server_live = true
    endif
  -%}
  <script>
    (function () {
      var start = {{ bf_start }} * 1000;
      if ({{ bf_server_live }} || (start > 0 && Date.now() >= start)) {
        document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-bf', 'live');
      }
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    html:not([data-bf='live']) [data-bf-on],
    html[data-bf='live'] [data-bf-off] {
      display: none !important;
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
